+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Clients send partial updates as JSON Merge Patch. Export `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` from
+`src/index.ts`, implementing RFC 7386 section 2 and returning the merged document.
+
+# What was done
+
+- `applyMergePatch` in `src/index.ts`: a non-object patch (primitive, array, `null`) replaces the target;
+  an object patch merges member by member into the target (or `{}` if the target is not an object); a
+  `null` member deletes the target member. Arrays are replaced wholesale.
+- Inputs are not mutated and the result shares no structure with them; members are defined, not assigned,
+  and only own target members are read, so `__proto__` cannot pollute prototypes.
+- Tests in `test/merge-patch.test.ts`: all RFC 7386 appendix A examples, non-mutation, prototype safety.
+  `npm test`: 91 pass, 0 fail.
+- `README.md` documents the new function.
